 "result": "Package is `src/tessel/` (a Flask-style framework). The order is:\n\n1. **`Tessel.__call__`** (`src/tessel/app.py:1618`) delegates to `wsgi_entry`.\n2. **`Tessel.wsgi_entry`** (`app.py:1566`) calls `request_context(environ)`, which calls **`AppContext.from_environ`** (`src/tessel/ctx.py:340`) to build the request and context.\n3. **`AppContext.push`** (`ctx.py:416`) does the following:\n   - sets the context var and sends `appcontext_pushed`;\n   - opens the session via `_get_session()`;\n   - calls **`AppContext.match_request`** (`ctx.py:405`), which runs `url_adapter.match()` and stores `url_rule` and `view_args`, or the routing exception.\n4. **`Tessel.run_full_request`** (`app.py:992`) does the following:\n   - sends `request_started`;\n   - calls **`preprocess_request`** (`app.py:1366`), which runs `url_value_preprocessors` and then `before_request_funcs`. A non-None return short-circuits the view.\n5. **`Tessel.run_view`** (`app.py`, called at line 1016) does the following:\n   - raises any stored routing exception;\n   - handles automatic `OPTIONS` via `make_default_options_response`;\n   - looks up `view_functions[rule.endpoint]`, wraps it with `ensure_sync`, and calls it with `**view_args` (`app.py:990`).\n\nAfter the view returns, `finalize_request` (`app.py:1021`) calls `make_response` and `finalize_reply`.",
